    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.extra\r\n\r\n### Question\r\n\r\nHello.\r\n\r\nI updated my plugs today. It appears that `Pick lsp scope='document_symbol'` now opens in a location list. Its the only lsp picker to do this. \r\n\r\nI bisected with my dotfiles and I did not find a change in my own configuration that caused this. Still possible, but wanted to drop a note here to see if anyone else is experiencing this? ",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.extra</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Hello.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I updated my plugs today. It appears that <code class=\"notranslate\">Pick lsp scope='document_symbol'</code> now opens in a location list. Its the only lsp picker to do this.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I bisected with my dotfiles and I did not find a change in my own configuration that caused this. Still possible, but wanted to drop a note here to see if anyone else is experiencing this?</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.extra\nQuestion\nHello.\nI updated my plugs today. It appears that Pick lsp scope='document_symbol' now opens in a location list. Its the only lsp picker to do this.\nI bisected with my dotfiles and I did not find a change in my own configuration that caused this. Still possible, but wanted to drop a note here to see if anyone else is experiencing this?",
